  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final rules require 55°C testing with a 5% failure limit but allow a 12-month corrective-action/retest pathway instead of immediate sales bans, and give per-model results to purchasers and regulators without public publication. Incident reporting requires 24-hour regulator notification for confirmed incidents and 72-hour customer notice for credible risks. Remote shut-off is required for new models only after 24 months, with no retrofit obligation and a six-year floor on any regulator-set deadline; fire suppression is required after 36 months, and S5 sets a mandatory recall at 8 incidents/100k but permits an open-ended, regulator-approved corrective-action alternative with prompt customer notices."
